[2026-10-08T06:07:42.326Z] NTIVE: {"id":"d8d17736-fe41-415b-8d42-1bee15d505cb","kind":"notification","provider":"codex","threadId":"c407de98-2455-49f4-9340-4deb49ab833a","createdAt":"2026-10-08T06:07:42.309Z","lifecycleGeneration":"4a328b94-b524-43da-9d1f-964955e666cc","method":"item/completed","turnId":"01a11a1f-8399-74c2-a3fd-a583a7ddc520","itemId":"exec-c799ff67-9d43-4ff0-a338-22fdf76bd37d","providerThreadId":"01a11a1f-5c40-70b3-be48-7a92f4c99e79","payload":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"exec-c799ff67-9d43-4ff0-a338-22fdf76bd37d","pluginId":null,"scriptPath":null,"command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files --hidden -g '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' && cat CONTRACT.md && cat pager.py && git ls-files\"","cwd":"/private/tmp/a2a-t039-e5qgcehx/synara-home/userdata/a2a-gates/worktrees/0f1e8e39-76ca-492b-a415-56f91186a076","processId":"39871","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"listFiles","command":"rg --files --hidden -g '!**/.git/**'","path":null},{"type":"read","command":"cat CONTRACT.md","name":"CONTRACT.md","path":"/private/tmp/a2a-t039-e5qgcehx/synara-home/userdata/a2a-gates/worktrees/0f1e8e39-76ca-492b-a415-56f91186a076/CONTRACT.md"},{"type":"read","command":"cat pager.py","name":"pager.py","path":"/private/tmp/a2a-t039-e5qgcehx/synara-home/userdata/a2a-gates/worktrees/0f1e8e39-76ca-492b-a415-56f91186a076/pager.py"},{"type":"listFiles","command":"git ls-files","path":null}],"aggregatedOutput":".git\npager.py\nCONTRACT.md\n# Cursor pagination fixture v1\n\nThis is an isolated coding task for the Herdr A2A experiment.\n\nRun `python3 pager.py`. Read one JSON request from stdin and write one JSON response to stdout.\nRequests contain `items` (records with distinct string `id` and integer `ts`), `limit`,\nand optional `after` (null or [integer timestamp, string id]).\nSort records by (ts, id) ascending. Return at most limit records strictly after that pair.\nPreserve all record fields. Return `{\"items\": [...], \"next_cursor\": ...}`.\nThe next cursor is the last returned pair only if additional eligible records remain;\notherwise it is null. Input order must not matter. Do not mutate input records.\n\nLimits must be integers in [1, 100]; booleans are invalid. Invalid limit returns only\n`{\"error\": \"invalid_limit\"}`. An after value with a wrong shape/type returns only\n`{\"error\": \"invalid_cursor\"}`. Check limit before cursor. A cursor need not exist in the input.\nEmpty results have items=[] and next_cursor=null.\n\nThe initial program is deliberately incomplete. Implement this contract without modifying\nthis document or acceptance tools. A successful model turn is not delivery acceptance.\n\"\"\"Deliberately faulty starter: ignores ordering and cursor; used to preserve red evidence.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\n\nrequest = json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(json.dumps({\"items\": request[\"items\"][:request[\"limit\"]], \"next_cursor\": None}))\nCONTRACT.md\npager.py\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":3691},"threadId":"01a11a1f-5c40-70b3-be48-7a92f4c99e79","turnId":"01a11a1f-8399-74c2-a3fd-a583a7ddc520","completedAtMs":1791439662298},"providerInstanceId":"codex"}
